   "models": "Impedance by formula (Hammerstad-Jensen, Wheeler, Wadell, IPC-2141); differential and coplanar lines can be off by 5\u201315 %. Losses: Wheeler/Huray/Djordjevic-Sarkar. Lanes run from device pin to device pin through series parts (estimated parasitics); side stubs of the lane nets are open stubs (unused pads, parts not fitted with their pad capacitance, the other path of a fork). Pads: a track inside an SMD pad has the pad's width; the rest of a part's pad is a capacitance from the pad's cross-section (with what lies below it), else an estimate per package. Eye: PRBS7, linear transmitter/receiver from the profile (a termination next to the receiver acts as its termination), without equalisation, jitter and noise; the step response with a DC point and checks (band edge, response before arrival, settling, passivity) in its warnings. Pairs are 4-ports (both lines on their own paths, coupled where they run together): loss and return loss Sdd21/Sdd11, the eye driven differentially, mode_conversion_db (worst Scd21 up to 1.5 \u00d7 Nyquist) as information. Multi-drop lines along one path: the eye at every receiver (receivers), the worst counts. One N-port Touchstone file behind a connector with a port map (connector_ends.<connector>.touchstone.ports): the connector's other lanes in it are worst-case aggressors (crosstalk_peak; they enter at the connector without their board traces \u2013 an estimate). Shunt parts on the lane's nets (capacitors to ground, \u2026) are in the channel at their pads. Lanes from connector to connector: board share only (loss, return loss, skew, TDR), no eye. Lanes ending at a connector: board share \u2013 loss, return loss and skew judged; the eye with the connector end model (kisi.json connector_ends.<connector>, default the profile's receiver or transmitter at the connector) \u2013 information (eye_board_share), or judged when a channel behind the connector (rest_loss_db or a Touchstone file) is given.",
